    "updated_at": "2026-11-27T01:08:55Z",
    "body": "fix on sn3ro:issue/3071-hobby-routers · PR #4263 · pinned by every_hobby_router_states_only_its_published_figures, every_tool_change_is_a_stop_after_a_lift_in_the_work_offset, the_shapeoko_4x4_two_tool_program_is_locked · merges at the next cut\n\nThe PR is a slice (`Refs #3071`). It adds the Shapeoko 5 Pro (4x4, 4x2, 2x2) and the X-Carve (2021 1000 mm, Pro 4x4, Pro 4x2). The Onefinity frames stay open on this issue:\n- The current Gen 2 Elite controller is \"Redline CNC Controller powered by Realtime CNC motion software\" (https://www.onefinitycnc.com/compare-product). No built-in post is confirmed for its dialect.\n- The compare page gives the figures for each series, not for each model. The series page fills its table by a script.\n- The figures that the compare page shows for the Gen 2 Elite: XY cutting area 838 x 838 mm (Woodworker), 1245 x 838 mm (Journeyman), 1245 x 1248 mm (Foreman); Z travel 163 mm; XY rapid 15240 mm/min; Z rapid 5715 mm/min.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
